WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:29.711
Mutation -- it is the key
to our evolution.

2
00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.964
It has enabled us to evolve
from a single-celled organism ...

3
00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.508
into the dominant species
on the planet.

4
00:00:35.593 --> 00:00:39.971
This process is slow, normally taking 
thousands and thousands of years.

5
00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:44.142
But every few hundred millennia,
evolution leaps forward.

6
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.202
Niagara Falls. Up ...

7
00:04:31.287 --> 00:04:36.582
the Canadian Rockies, and then it's 
only a few hundred miles to Anchorage.

8
00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.710
Well, won't it be kind of cold?

9
00:04:38.794 --> 00:04:40.712
Well, that's the point, stupid.

10
00:04:40.796 --> 00:04:43.006
Otherwise, it wouldn't
be an adventure.

11
00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.675
And when are you gonna do this?

12
00:04:48.929 --> 00:04:51.639
I don't know.

13
00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.059
After high school. Before college.

14
00:05:39.396 --> 00:05:42.065
Marie! David?
I don't know what happened to him.

15
00:05:42.149 --> 00:05:45.526
I don't know what --
I just touched him.

16
00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.695
I didn't --
I didn't mean --

17
00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.781
- Call an ambulance!
- Don't touch.

18
00:05:49.865 --> 00:05:52.825
- Honey --
- Just get away from me!
- Call an ambulance!

19
00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.161
Don't touch me!

20
00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:58.414
Ladies and gentlemen,

21
00:05:58.499 --> 00:06:01.417
we are now seeing the beginnings 
of another stage of human evolution.

22
00:06:01.502 --> 00:06:04.379
These mutations
manifest at puberty ...

23
00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:08.549
and are often triggered by periods 
of heightened emotional stress.

24
00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.302
Thank you, Ms. Grey.
It was quite educational.

25
00:06:11.387 --> 00:06:15.973
However, it fails to address the issue 
that is the focus of this hearing.

26
00:06:16.058 --> 00:06:19.644
Three words: Are mutants dangerous?

27
00:06:19.728 --> 00:06:22.647
I'm afraid that's an unfair 
question, Senator Kelly.

28
00:06:22.731 --> 00:06:25.566
After all, the wrong person behind 
the wheel of a car can be dangerous.

29
00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.610
Well, we do license people to drive.

30
00:06:27.694 --> 00:06:31.656
Yes, but not to live.
Senator, it is a fact ...

31
00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.201
that mutants who have come forward 
and revealed themselves publicly ...

32
00:06:35.285 --> 00:06:38.913
have been met with fear,
hostility, even violence.

33
00:06:38.997 --> 00:06:41.499
It is because of that
ever-present hostility ...

34
00:06:41.583 --> 00:06:45.128
that I am urging the Senate to 
vote against mutant registration.

35
00:06:45.212 --> 00:06:49.382
- To force mutants to expose
  themselves will only further --
- Expose themselves?

36
00:06:49.466 --> 00:06:52.051
What is it the mutant community
has to hide I wonder ...

37
00:06:52.136 --> 00:06:54.137
that makes them so afraid
to identify themselves?

38
00:06:54.263 --> 00:06:58.099
I didn't say they were hiding.
Let me show you what
is being hidden, Ms. Grey.

39
00:06:58.183 --> 00:07:01.936
I have here a list of names
of identified mutants ...

40
00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:03.938
living right here in the United States.

41
00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:08.317
- Senator Kelly --
- Now, here's a girl in Illinois
  who can walk through walls.

42
00:07:08.402 --> 00:07:11.112
Now, what's to stop her from 
walking into a bank vault ...

43
00:07:11.196 --> 00:07:14.282
or into the White House
or into their houses?

44
00:07:14.408 --> 00:07:16.617
Senator Kelly --
And there are even rumors, Ms. Grey,

45
00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:21.789
of mutants so powerful that they can 
enter our minds and control our thoughts,

46
00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:24.625
taking our God-given free will.

47
00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:27.837
I think the American people
deserve the right to decide ...

48
00:07:27.921 --> 00:07:30.715
whether they want their children
to be in school with mutants,

49
00:07:30.799 --> 00:07:32.675
to be taught by mutants.

50
00:07:34.595 --> 00:07:37.305
Ladies and gentlemen,

51
00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:40.516
the truth is that 
mutants are very real,

52
00:07:40.601 --> 00:07:43.478
and they are among us.

53
00:07:43.604 --> 00:07:46.272
- We must know who they are,
- That's right!

54
00:07:46.356 --> 00:07:48.232
And, above all, we must know ...

55
00:07:48.317 --> 00:07:50.526
what they can do.

56
00:08:14.176 --> 00:08:16.093
Eric.

57
00:08:18.639 --> 00:08:22.058
- What are you doing here?
- Why do you ask questions ...

58
00:08:22.142 --> 00:08:24.185
to which you already
know the answers?

59
00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:27.396
Don't give up on them, Eric.

60
00:08:27.481 --> 00:08:31.943
What would you have me do, Charles? 
I've heard these arguments before.

61
00:08:32.027 --> 00:08:35.154
It was a long time ago.

62
00:08:35.239 --> 00:08:37.406
Mankind has evolved since then.

63
00:08:37.491 --> 00:08:38.950
Yes,

64
00:08:39.034 --> 00:08:41.118
into us.

65
00:08:47.459 --> 00:08:49.377
You sneaking around in here, Charles?

66
00:08:49.461 --> 00:08:52.088
Whatever are you looking for?

67
00:08:59.596 --> 00:09:01.556
I'm looking for hope.

68
00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:05.059
I will bring you hope, old friend.

69
00:09:05.143 --> 00:09:08.980
And I ask
only one thing in return.

70
00:09:10.941 --> 00:09:12.858
Don't get in my way.

71
00:09:15.696 --> 00:09:19.240
We are the future, 
Charles, not them.

72
00:09:19.324 --> 00:09:21.450
They no longer matter.

73
00:09:35.424 --> 00:09:37.341
This is it.

74
00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.767
Where are we?

75
00:09:46.852 --> 00:09:49.854
I thought you said you were gonna 
take me as far as Laughlin City.

76
00:09:49.938 --> 00:09:51.856
This is Laughlin City.

77
00:10:23.639 --> 00:10:26.182
Gentlemen, in all my years,

78
00:10:26.266 --> 00:10:28.434
I've never seen anything like that.

79
00:10:30.562 --> 00:10:34.649
Are you gonna let this man
walk away with your money?

80
00:10:34.733 --> 00:10:36.734
I'll fight him!

81
00:10:40.739 --> 00:10:45.576
Ladies and gentlemen, our savior!

82
00:10:47.037 --> 00:10:49.038
Whatever you do,
don't hit him in the balls.

83
00:10:49.164 --> 00:10:53.125
You said anything goes.
Anything goes, but 
he'll take it personal.

84
00:11:17.943 --> 00:11:21.862
Ladies and gentlemen,

85
00:11:21.947 --> 00:11:25.908
tonight's winner
and still king of the cage,

86
00:11:25.992 --> 00:11:27.910
the Wolverine!

87
00:11:56.356 --> 00:11:58.482
You want something new, honey?

88
00:11:59.901 --> 00:12:02.653
Or are you sticking with water?

89
00:12:11.496 --> 00:12:13.456
I'll have a beer.

90
00:12:23.008 --> 00:12:27.428
Ellis Island, once the arrival point 
for thousands of American immigrants ...

91
00:12:27.512 --> 00:12:29.430
is opening its doors again.

92
00:12:29.514 --> 00:12:33.434
Preparations are nearly
completed for the upcoming
United Nations world summit.

93
00:12:33.518 --> 00:12:35.561
With nearly
every invitation confirmed,

94
00:12:35.645 --> 00:12:40.775
the event promises to be
the largest single gathering
of world leaders in history.

95
00:12:40.859 --> 00:12:45.446
The leaders of over 200 nations
will discuss issues ranging from
the world's economic climate ...

96
00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:50.159
and weapons treaties
to the mutant phenomenon and
its impact on our world stage.

97
00:12:50.243 --> 00:12:53.287
Many American legislators
have contended ...

98
00:12:53.371 --> 00:12:57.458
that debate over mutant issues
should be the primary focus
of what is, on the surface,

99
00:12:57.542 --> 00:13:00.503
a strictly diplomatic affair.

100
00:13:00.629 --> 00:13:03.589
You owe me some money.
Come on, Stu. Let's not do this.

101
00:13:03.673 --> 00:13:08.093
No man takes a beating like that
without a mark to show for it.

102
00:13:08.178 --> 00:13:10.721
Come on, buddy.
This isn't gonna be worth it.

103
00:13:10.847 --> 00:13:13.849
I know what you are. You lost your money. 
Keep this up, you'll lose something else.

104
00:13:13.934 --> 00:13:15.559
Come on, buddy.

105
00:13:17.604 --> 00:13:18.854
Look out!

106
00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:34.537
Get out of my bar, freak.

107
00:15:23.521 --> 00:15:27.441
- What the hell are you doing?
- I'm sorry. I needed a ride.

108
00:15:27.525 --> 00:15:30.027
- Thought you might help me.
- Get out.

109
00:15:31.488 --> 00:15:34.073
- Where am I supposed to go?
- I don't know.

110
00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:36.742
You don't know or you don't care?
Pick one.

111
00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.832
- I saved your life.
- No, you didn't.

112
00:15:59.099 --> 00:16:01.558
You don't have anything
to eat, do you?

113
00:16:22.747 --> 00:16:24.707
I'm Rogue.

114
00:16:30.338 --> 00:16:32.589
Were you in the army?

115
00:16:32.674 --> 00:16:35.092
Doesn't that mean
you were in the army?

116
00:16:42.392 --> 00:16:44.268
- Wow.
- What?

117
00:16:48.106 --> 00:16:50.899
- Suddenly my life 
  doesn't look that bad.
- If you'd prefer the road --

118
00:16:50.984 --> 00:16:54.445
No. No. It looks great.

119
00:16:57.449 --> 00:17:00.242
Looks cozy.

120
00:17:06.624 --> 00:17:08.959
Put your hands on the heater.

121
00:17:10.128 --> 00:17:12.504
I'm not gonna hurt you, kid.

122
00:17:12.589 --> 00:17:15.299
It's nothing personal.
It's just that ...

123
00:17:15.383 --> 00:17:17.468
when people touch my skin,
something happens.

124
00:17:17.594 --> 00:17:21.305
What?
I don't know.

125
00:17:21.389 --> 00:17:23.724
They just get hurt.

126
00:17:23.808 --> 00:17:25.768
Fair enough.

127
00:17:29.898 --> 00:17:33.358
When they come out, does it hurt?

128
00:17:36.404 --> 00:17:38.322
Every time.

129
00:17:41.451 --> 00:17:44.203
So, what kind of a name
is Rogue?

130
00:17:46.331 --> 00:17:49.666
I don't know. What kind
of a name is Wolverine?

131
00:17:53.797 --> 00:17:55.714
My name's Logan.

132
00:17:57.717 --> 00:17:59.676
Marie.

133
00:18:01.805 --> 00:18:04.598
You know, you should wear
your seat belt.

134
00:18:04.682 --> 00:18:06.850
Look, kid. I don't need advice
on auto safety from --

135
00:19:12.792 --> 00:19:15.544
You all right?

136
00:19:15.628 --> 00:19:17.588
- Kid, are you all right?
- I'm stuck!

137
00:21:03.486 --> 00:21:08.490
Weren't you supposed to bring
someone back with you?

138
00:21:20.044 --> 00:21:22.254
- What happened?
- They knew.

139
00:21:31.097 --> 00:21:33.015
Charles.

140
00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:43.650
Hmm.

141
00:21:45.737 --> 00:21:48.238
- Where is the mutant now?
- With them.

142
00:21:50.992 --> 00:21:53.577
I have made the first move.

143
00:21:54.746 --> 00:21:57.497
That is all they know.

144
00:21:57.582 --> 00:22:00.459
Come. The U.N. Summit
is approaching.

145
00:22:00.543 --> 00:22:02.627
Time for our little test.

146
00:23:13.324 --> 00:23:15.283
Where's he going?

147
00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:44.813
Where are you going?

148
00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:52.529
Over here.

149
00:24:20.141 --> 00:24:22.058
Where are you going?
This way.

150
00:24:22.143 --> 00:24:24.060
He's over there.

151
00:24:31.068 --> 00:24:33.403
- Let's go.
- What's your hurry?

152
00:24:57.595 --> 00:25:00.597
Good morning, Logan.

153
00:25:00.681 --> 00:25:03.517
I'd like your definitions of weak 
and strong anthropic principle ...

154
00:25:03.601 --> 00:25:05.519
on my desk on Wednesday.

155
00:25:05.603 --> 00:25:07.604
That'll be all.

156
00:25:13.986 --> 00:25:16.279
Bye, Professor.
Bye, Kitty.

157
00:25:20.159 --> 00:25:22.118
Physics.

158
00:25:23.496 --> 00:25:25.705
I'm Charles Xavier.
Would you like some breakfast?

159
00:25:25.790 --> 00:25:30.043
- Where am I?
- Westchester, New York.

160
00:25:30.127 --> 00:25:34.256
You were attacked. My people brought 
you here for medical attention.

161
00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:37.592
- I don't need medical attention.
- Yes, of course.

162
00:25:40.096 --> 00:25:42.597
- Where's the girl?
- Rogue? She's here. She's fine.

163
00:25:42.682 --> 00:25:45.392
Really.

164
00:25:45.476 --> 00:25:51.314
Ah, Logan, I'd like you to meet 
Ororo Monroe, also called Storm.

165
00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:54.609
This is Scott Summers, also called Cyclops.
Hello.

166
00:25:57.572 --> 00:26:00.615
They saved your life.

167
00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:03.451
I believe you've already
met Dr. Jean Grey.

168
00:26:04.996 --> 00:26:07.581
You're in my school for the gifted.
For mutants.

169
00:26:07.665 --> 00:26:11.167
- You'll be safe here
  from Magneto.
- What's a Magneto?

170
00:26:11.252 --> 00:26:14.921
A very powerful mutant who 
believes that a war is brewin ...

171
00:26:15.006 --> 00:26:17.799
between mutants and
the rest of humanity.

172
00:26:17.883 --> 00:26:19.843
I've been following his 
activities for some time.

173
00:26:19.927 --> 00:26:22.679
The man who attacked you is an 
associate of his called Sabretooth.

174
00:26:22.763 --> 00:26:24.806
Sabretooth?

175
00:26:25.850 --> 00:26:29.477
Storm.

176
00:26:29.562 --> 00:26:32.188
What do they call you? Wheels?

177
00:26:33.399 --> 00:26:36.192
This is the stupidest
thing I've ever heard.

178
00:26:39.697 --> 00:26:43.992
Cyclops, right?
You wanna get out of my way?

179
00:26:45.870 --> 00:26:49.539
Logan, It's been almost
15 years, hasn't it?

180
00:26:49.624 --> 00:26:53.460
Living from day to day,
moving from place to place,

181
00:26:53.544 --> 00:26:56.630
with no memory
of who or what you are.

182
00:26:56.714 --> 00:26:58.632
Shut up.

183
00:26:58.716 --> 00:27:00.675
Give me a chance.

184
00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:04.179
I may be able to help you
find some answers.

185
00:27:04.263 --> 00:27:06.640
How do you know?

186
00:27:06.724 --> 00:27:08.892
You're not the only one with gifts.

187
00:27:08.976 --> 00:27:10.935
Where are you going?
Where's he going?

188
00:27:11.020 --> 00:27:13.521
What are you doing there?

189
00:27:17.652 --> 00:27:19.569
What is this place?

190
00:27:21.280 --> 00:27:24.240
Anonymity is
a mutant's first chance ...

191
00:27:24.325 --> 00:27:26.242
against the world's hostility.

192
00:27:26.327 --> 00:27:29.162
Hey, no powers!

193
00:27:29.246 --> 00:27:32.082
To the public, we're merely a 
school for gifted youngsters.

194
00:27:33.501 --> 00:27:37.170
Cyclops, Storm and Jean
were some of my first students.

195
00:27:37.254 --> 00:27:41.508
I protected them, taught them
to control their powers ...

196
00:27:41.592 --> 00:27:45.845
and in time,
teach others to do the same.

197
00:27:45.930 --> 00:27:47.889
The students are mostly runaways.

198
00:27:47.973 --> 00:27:50.016
Frightened, alone.

199
00:27:50.101 --> 00:27:52.686
Some with gifts so extreme
that they've become a danger ...

200
00:27:52.770 --> 00:27:55.063
to themselves
and those around them.

201
00:27:55.147 --> 00:27:57.607
Like your friend, Rogue.

202
00:27:57.692 --> 00:28:00.694
Incapable of physical human contact, 
probably for the rest of her life,

203
00:28:00.778 --> 00:28:04.489
and yet here she is
with others her own age,

204
00:28:04.573 --> 00:28:08.034
learning being accepted,
not feared.

205
00:28:19.255 --> 00:28:21.256
- John.
- Sorry.

206
00:28:26.470 --> 00:28:28.888
I'm Bobby. What's your name?

207
00:28:28.973 --> 00:28:32.475
- Rogue.
- What'll happen to her?

208
00:28:32.560 --> 00:28:36.479
Well, that's up to her. Rejoin the 
world as an educated young woman ...

209
00:28:36.564 --> 00:28:38.982
or stay on to teach others ...

210
00:28:39.066 --> 00:28:41.401
to become what the children have 
affectionately called X-Men.

211
00:28:41.485 --> 00:28:44.487
Welcome to Mutant High.

212
00:28:45.990 --> 00:28:48.324
But the school is 
merely a public face.

213
00:28:48.409 --> 00:28:52.454
The lower levels, however, are
an entirely different matter.

214
00:28:57.668 --> 00:29:02.380
When I was a boy, I discovered I had 
the power to control people's minds,

215
00:29:02.465 --> 00:29:05.383
make them think or do
whatever I wanted.

216
00:29:05.468 --> 00:29:09.596
When I was 17, I met a young 
man named Eric Lensherr.

217
00:29:09.680 --> 00:29:11.931
He, too, had an unusual power.

218
00:29:12.016 --> 00:29:15.977
He could create magnetic 
fields and control metal.

219
00:29:16.061 --> 00:29:18.271
Believing that humanity
would never accept us,

220
00:29:18.355 --> 00:29:21.524
he grew angry and vengeful.

221
00:29:22.860 --> 00:29:24.819
He became Magneto.

222
00:29:26.405 --> 00:29:30.116
There are mutants out there
with incredible powers, Logan,

223
00:29:30.201 --> 00:29:33.828
and many who do not share
my respect for mankind.

224
00:29:33.913 --> 00:29:38.291
If no one is equipped to oppose them, 
humanity's days could be over.

225
00:29:38.375 --> 00:29:40.543
I'll make a deal with you, Logan.

226
00:29:40.628 --> 00:29:44.631
Give me 48 hours to find out 
what Magneto wants with you,

227
00:29:44.715 --> 00:29:47.884
and I give you my word that I 
will use all my power ...

228
00:29:47.968 --> 00:29:50.637
to help you piece together
what you've lost ...

229
00:29:50.721 --> 00:29:53.181
and what you're looking for.

230
00:30:21.043 --> 00:30:24.045
Senator, listen, you favor
gun registration, yes?

231
00:30:24.129 --> 00:30:26.172
Well, some of these
so-called children ...

232
00:30:26.257 --> 00:30:30.802
possess more than 10 times the 
destructive force of any handgun.

233
00:30:30.886 --> 00:30:34.556
No, I don't see a difference.
All I see are weapons in our schools.

234
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:37.517
Well, that's fair enough.
All right.

235
00:30:37.601 --> 00:30:39.727
So?

236
00:30:39.812 --> 00:30:44.023
It's gonna be close.
A vote this loaded is always close.

237
00:30:44.108 --> 00:30:47.360
What about the U.N. Summit?
The whole world will be watching.

238
00:30:47.444 --> 00:30:49.904
Maybe there's some way you could 
use that to your advantage.

239
00:30:49.989 --> 00:30:51.948
We're Americans, Henry.

240
00:30:52.032 --> 00:30:54.701
Let the rest of the damn world deal
with mutants in their own way.

241
00:30:54.785 --> 00:30:57.203
You know this situation?

242
00:30:57.288 --> 00:30:59.789
These mutants?

243
00:30:59.874 --> 00:31:01.916
People like this Jean Grey?

244
00:31:03.502 --> 00:31:06.713
If it were up to me,
I'd lock 'em all away.

245
00:31:06.797 --> 00:31:12.176
It's a war. It's the reason
people like me exist.

246
00:31:19.977 --> 00:31:22.437
Where the hell are we?

247
00:31:32.156 --> 00:31:34.324
Pilot!

248
00:31:37.077 --> 00:31:40.496
People like you are the reason I was 
afraid to go to school as a child.

249
00:32:13.197 --> 00:32:16.783
- I'm sorry.
- For what?

250
00:32:16.867 --> 00:32:19.160
If I hurt you.

251
00:32:28.212 --> 00:32:32.674
So, couldn't wait to get
my shirt off again, huh?

252
00:32:49.400 --> 00:32:52.026
The metal is an alloy
called adamantium.

253
00:32:52.111 --> 00:32:57.824
Supposedly indestructible.
It's been surgically grafted
to his entire skeleton.

254
00:32:57.908 --> 00:33:01.285
How could he have survived
a procedure like that?

255
00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:05.248
His mutation. He has uncharted
regenerative capability,

256
00:33:05.332 --> 00:33:08.209
which enables him
to heal rapidly.

257
00:33:08.293 --> 00:33:12.130
This also makes his age
impossible to determine.

258
00:33:12.214 --> 00:33:14.841
He could very well be older 
than you, Professor.

259
00:33:16.176 --> 00:33:19.012
Who did this to him?
He doesn't know.

260
00:33:19.096 --> 00:33:22.640
Nor does he remember anything 
about his life before it happened.

261
00:33:22.725 --> 00:33:25.351
Experimentation on mutants.

262
00:33:25.436 --> 00:33:27.437
It's not unheard of.

263
00:33:27.521 --> 00:33:30.732
But I've never seen
anything like this before.

264
00:33:30.816 --> 00:33:33.484
What do you think
Magneto wants with him?

265
00:33:33.569 --> 00:33:37.613
I'm not entirely sure
it's him Magneto wants.

266
00:33:59.428 --> 00:34:01.345
Yech!

267
00:34:01.430 --> 00:34:03.931
Toad has a wicked tongue, Senator.

268
00:34:04.016 --> 00:34:06.476
Just like you.

269
00:34:13.650 --> 00:34:16.027
Who are you people?
Where's Henry?

270
00:34:16.111 --> 00:34:19.697
Mr. Guyrich has been dead
for some time, Senator.

271
00:34:19.782 --> 00:34:22.575
But I've had Mystique here
keep you company.

272
00:34:22.659 --> 00:34:24.577
She takes so many shapes.

273
00:34:24.661 --> 00:34:28.247
Whatever you do to me,
you'll make me right.

274
00:34:28.332 --> 00:34:32.210
Every word I've spoken
will be confirmed.

275
00:34:35.172 --> 00:34:37.507
Are you a God-fearing man, Senator?

276
00:34:37.591 --> 00:34:40.593
That's such a strange phrase.

277
00:34:40.677 --> 00:34:43.429
I've always thought
of God as a teacher,

278
00:34:43.514 --> 00:34:47.016
as a bringer of light, wisdom
and understanding.

279
00:34:47.101 --> 00:34:52.814
You see, I think what you really
are afraid of is me.

280
00:34:52.898 --> 00:34:56.025
Me and my kind.
The Brotherhood of Mutants.

281
00:34:58.487 --> 00:35:00.905
Though it's not
so surprising, really.

282
00:35:00.989 --> 00:35:05.535
Mankind has always feared
what it doesn't understand.

283
00:35:07.162 --> 00:35:10.164
Well, don't fear God, Senator,

284
00:35:10.249 --> 00:35:12.208
and certainly, don't fear me.

285
00:35:13.335 --> 00:35:15.253
Not anymore.

286
00:35:17.381 --> 00:35:19.382
What do you intend to do to me?

287
00:35:19.466 --> 00:35:22.885
Let's just say God works too slowly.

288
00:36:38.462 --> 00:36:40.713
I think you'll be comfortable here.

289
00:36:40.797 --> 00:36:44.008
- Where is your room?
- With Scott down the hall.

290
00:36:45.469 --> 00:36:48.846
Is that your gift?
Putting up with that guy?

291
00:36:48.931 --> 00:36:52.558
Actually, I'm telekinetic.
I can move things with my mind.

292
00:36:52.643 --> 00:36:54.810
Really? What kinds of things?

293
00:36:56.355 --> 00:36:59.148
All kinds of things.

294
00:36:59.233 --> 00:37:02.026
I also have some
telepathic ability.

295
00:37:02.110 --> 00:37:05.529
- What, like your Professor?
- Nowhere near that powerful.

296
00:37:05.614 --> 00:37:08.407
But he's teaching me to develop it.

297
00:37:08.492 --> 00:37:10.451
I'm sure he is.

298
00:37:12.496 --> 00:37:14.747
- So read my mind.
- I'd rather not.

299
00:37:14.831 --> 00:37:17.333
Come on.
You afraid you might like it?

300
00:37:17.417 --> 00:37:19.335
I doubt it.

301
00:37:40.357 --> 00:37:41.983
What do you see?

302
00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:45.861
Scott.

303
00:37:48.782 --> 00:37:51.075
Good night, Logan.

304
00:38:00.002 --> 00:38:01.919
You gonna tell me
to stay away from your girl?

305
00:38:02.004 --> 00:38:04.255
If I had to do that,
she wouldn't be my girl.

306
00:38:04.339 --> 00:38:07.925
Hmm. Well, then, I guess you've 
got nothing to worry about,

307
00:38:08.010 --> 00:38:09.885
do you, Cyclops?

308
00:38:09.970 --> 00:38:14.307
Yeah, it must just burn you up that 
a boy like me saved your life, huh?

309
00:38:14.391 --> 00:38:16.892
You ought to be careful.
I might not be there next time.

310
00:38:16.977 --> 00:38:20.104
Oh, and, Logan,

311
00:38:20.188 --> 00:38:22.732
stay away from my girl.

312
00:38:56.141 --> 00:38:58.476
Logan.

313
00:39:07.569 --> 00:39:10.738
Logan. Logan, wake up.

314
00:39:42.771 --> 00:39:46.023
Help me.

315
00:39:48.902 --> 00:39:51.862
Somebody help!

316
00:40:22.561 --> 00:40:24.812
Scott, grab a pillow.

317
00:40:27.065 --> 00:40:29.817
It was an accident.

318
00:40:38.743 --> 00:40:42.037
- Logan?
- What happened?

319
00:40:43.373 --> 00:40:46.000
- Is she all right?
- She'll be all right.

320
00:40:48.170 --> 00:40:50.087
What did she do to me?

321
00:40:50.172 --> 00:40:53.966
Whenever Rogue touches someone, she 
takes their energy, their life force.

322
00:40:54.050 --> 00:40:57.970
In the case of mutants, she absorbs 
their gifts for a short while.

323
00:40:58.054 --> 00:41:00.556
In your case, your ability to heal.

324
00:41:02.934 --> 00:41:04.935
I feel like she almost killed me.

325
00:41:05.020 --> 00:41:08.189
If she'd held out any longer,
she could have.

326
00:42:03.703 --> 00:42:06.914
How are we feeling, Senator?
Advanced, I hope.

327
00:42:08.792 --> 00:42:10.751
Hmm.

328
00:42:24.516 --> 00:42:26.934
What the hell have you done to me?

329
00:42:27.018 --> 00:42:31.063
Senator, this is pointless.
Where would you go?

330
00:42:31.147 --> 00:42:33.774
Who would take you in
now that you're one of us?

331
00:43:30.415 --> 00:43:34.835
Tommy, let it go!
Tommy, please let it go!

332
00:43:34.919 --> 00:43:36.879
I'm telling Mommy.

333
00:43:51.227 --> 00:43:53.896
Is that a mutant?

334
00:43:59.069 --> 00:44:00.986
... of this week's U.N. Summit.

335
00:44:01.071 --> 00:44:03.489
With the leaders
of over 200 nations attending,

336
00:44:03.573 --> 00:44:06.492
the Secret Service
has transformed Ellis Island ...

337
00:44:06.576 --> 00:44:10.037
into a veritable Fort Knox for 
tomorrow night's opening gala.

338
00:44:10.121 --> 00:44:13.749
Ellis Island rests less than one 
mile from the shores of Manhattan.

339
00:44:15.335 --> 00:44:17.211
Rogue.

340
00:44:17.337 --> 00:44:21.215
Bobby. Rogue, what did you do?

341
00:44:22.592 --> 00:44:24.593
They say that you're
stealing other mutants' powers.

342
00:44:24.678 --> 00:44:26.679
No, no. I borrowed his powers.

343
00:44:26.763 --> 00:44:30.057
You never use your power
against another mutant.

344
00:44:32.143 --> 00:44:34.561
I had no choice.

345
00:44:34.688 --> 00:44:36.730
No, you have to understand me.
If I were you,

346
00:44:36.815 --> 00:44:39.274
I'd get myself out of here.

347
00:44:41.695 --> 00:44:45.572
What do you mean?
Listen, the students are freaked.

348
00:44:45.657 --> 00:44:48.617
Professor Xavier's furious.
I don't know what he'll do with you.

349
00:44:52.247 --> 00:44:54.915
I think it'll be easier
on your own.

350
00:45:00.839 --> 00:45:03.090
You should go.

351
00:45:26.322 --> 00:45:28.282
What are you looking for, Eric?

352
00:45:28.366 --> 00:45:33.245
It's strange. There are more 
powerful mutants out there.

353
00:45:33.329 --> 00:45:35.456
Why should this one
be so important to him?

354
00:45:35.582 --> 00:45:37.958
Maybe it's his way with people.
You don't like him.

355
00:45:39.419 --> 00:45:43.005
- How could you tell?
- Well, I am psychic, you know.

356
00:45:44.424 --> 00:45:46.300
- Where is she?
- Who?

357
00:45:46.384 --> 00:45:48.343
Rogue.

358
00:45:48.428 --> 00:45:50.345
She's gone.

359
00:45:54.893 --> 00:45:57.519
Welcome, Professor.

360
00:46:00.356 --> 00:46:02.649
Welcome to Cerebro.

361
00:46:07.197 --> 00:46:10.824
This certainly is
a big, round room.

362
00:46:10.909 --> 00:46:14.495
The brain waves of mutants are 
different from average human beings.

363
00:46:14.579 --> 00:46:16.497
This device amplifies my power,

364
00:46:16.581 --> 00:46:19.291
allowing me to locate mutants
across great distances.

365
00:46:19.375 --> 00:46:22.294
That's how I intend to find Rogue.

366
00:46:22.420 --> 00:46:25.380
Why don't you just use it to find 
Magneto? I've been trying.

367
00:46:25.465 --> 00:46:29.134
But he seems to have found some 
way to shield himself from it.

368
00:46:29.219 --> 00:46:32.471
How would he know how to do that?

369
00:46:32.555 --> 00:46:35.599
Because he helped me build it.

370
00:46:35.683 --> 00:46:38.227
Now, if you'll excuse me.

371
00:46:50.281 --> 00:46:52.699
Have you eve --

372
00:46:52.784 --> 00:46:54.993
Used Cerebro?

373
00:46:55.078 --> 00:46:58.622
No. It takes
a degree of control,

374
00:46:58.706 --> 00:47:02.334
and, uh,
for someone like me, it's --

375
00:47:02.418 --> 00:47:04.378
Dangerous.

376
00:47:41.875 --> 00:47:45.085
... now boarding on track four.

377
00:47:48.756 --> 00:47:51.383
- She's at the train station.
- Where is it?

378
00:47:51.467 --> 00:47:54.720
A few miles west of here. Logan, 
you can't leave the mansion.

379
00:47:54.804 --> 00:47:59.057
- It's just the opportunity
  Magneto needs.
- I'm the reason she took off.

380
00:47:59.142 --> 00:48:03.312
- We had a deal.
- She's all right. She's just upset.

381
00:48:03.396 --> 00:48:05.647
Storm, Cyclops, find her.
See if you can talk to her.

382
00:48:15.909 --> 00:48:19.328
What? Where's my motorcycle?

383
00:48:56.074 --> 00:48:58.200
Hey, kid.

384
00:49:12.966 --> 00:49:14.883
I'm sorry about last night.

385
00:49:16.386 --> 00:49:18.345
Me too.

386
00:49:20.264 --> 00:49:25.644
- You running again?
- I heard the professor
  was mad at me.

387
00:49:25.728 --> 00:49:29.856
- Well, who told you that?
- A boy at school.

388
00:49:29.983 --> 00:49:33.402
When's the last time you saw her?
She was supposed to meet me for lunch.

389
00:49:39.117 --> 00:49:42.119
You look around. I'll check with
the ticket agent.

390
00:49:55.591 --> 00:49:57.551
Welcome, Professor.

391
00:50:22.535 --> 00:50:26.747
- You think I should go back.
- No, I think you should
  follow your instincts.

392
00:50:32.712 --> 00:50:35.338
The first boy I ever kissed ...

393
00:50:35.423 --> 00:50:38.967
ended up in a coma
for three weeks.

394
00:50:41.179 --> 00:50:43.764
I can still feel him inside my head.

395
00:50:46.142 --> 00:50:48.477
And it's the same with you.

396
00:51:15.171 --> 00:51:19.466
There's not many people
that'll understand what
you're going through,

397
00:51:19.550 --> 00:51:23.762
but I think this guy's
Xavier's one of them.

398
00:51:23.846 --> 00:51:27.140
He seems to genuinely
wanna help you,

399
00:51:27.225 --> 00:51:29.518
and that's a rare thing ...

400
00:51:31.104 --> 00:51:33.355
for people like us.

401
00:51:44.534 --> 00:51:47.119
So, what do you say?

402
00:51:47.203 --> 00:51:50.497
Give these geeks one more shot?

403
00:51:52.083 --> 00:51:54.000
Come on. I'll take care of you.

404
00:51:56.671 --> 00:51:59.631
- You promise?
- Yeah.

405
00:51:59.715 --> 00:52:01.675
Yeah, I promise.

406
00:52:14.897 --> 00:52:16.898
Come along now.

407
00:52:18.734 --> 00:52:22.154
She's about 17. Uh, my height.

408
00:52:22.238 --> 00:52:25.365
Has brown hair, and she-

409
00:52:31.747 --> 00:52:34.749
Scream for me.

410
00:53:19.837 --> 00:53:22.631
Quit playing around.

411
00:54:04.173 --> 00:54:06.466
You must be Wolverine.

412
00:54:08.177 --> 00:54:11.846
That remarkable metal doesn't run 
through your entire body, does it?

413
00:54:24.360 --> 00:54:27.362
Stop! Stop it!

414
00:54:27.446 --> 00:54:30.323
What the hell do you want with me?

415
00:54:30.408 --> 00:54:34.661
You? My dear boy,
whoever said I wanted you?

416
00:54:56.225 --> 00:54:58.143
Young people.

417
00:55:09.905 --> 00:55:12.073
All right, hold it.
Hold it right there.

418
00:55:12.158 --> 00:55:15.243
Stay where you are. Put your 
hands over your heads now.

419
00:55:47.777 --> 00:55:51.279
You Homo sapiens
and your guns.

420
00:55:55.117 --> 00:55:57.619
- That's enough, Eric.
- Let them go.

421
00:56:03.084 --> 00:56:06.211
Why not come out where
I can see you, Charles?

422
00:56:09.340 --> 00:56:11.257
- What do you --
- Want her for?

423
00:56:12.301 --> 00:56:15.261
Can't you read my mind?

424
00:56:16.722 --> 00:56:20.392
What now?
Save the girl?

425
00:56:20.476 --> 00:56:24.979
You'll have to kill me, Charles.
And what will that accomplish?

426
00:56:25.064 --> 00:56:28.942
Let them pass that law. They'll
have you in chains with a number
burned into your forehead.

427
00:56:29.026 --> 00:56:31.236
- It won't be --
- That way.

428
00:56:31.320 --> 00:56:33.488
Then kill me and find out.

429
00:56:36.158 --> 00:56:39.285
Huh? Then release me.

430
00:56:47.503 --> 00:56:49.462
Fine.

431
00:57:02.435 --> 00:57:04.769
Care to press your luck,
Charles?

432
00:57:09.358 --> 00:57:13.027
I don't think I can stop them all.

433
00:57:27.376 --> 00:57:29.419
Still unwilling
to make sacrifices.

434
00:57:29.503 --> 00:57:32.589
That's what makes you weak.

435
00:57:44.351 --> 00:57:46.895
Good-bye, Charles.

436
00:58:16.926 --> 00:58:18.384
You said he wanted me.

437
00:58:18.594 --> 00:58:20.386
I made a terrible mistake.

438
00:58:20.471 --> 00:58:23.973
His helmet was somehow designed
to block my telepathy.

439
00:58:25.559 --> 00:58:28.853
I couldn't see what he was after
till it was too late.

440
00:58:28.979 --> 00:58:31.064
Where are you going?
I'm gonna find her.

441
00:58:31.190 --> 00:58:34.317
How?
The traditional way. Look.

442
00:58:37.655 --> 00:58:40.156
Logan, you can't do this alone.

443
00:58:40.241 --> 00:58:43.201
Who's gonna help me?
You? So far you've
all done a bang-up job.

444
00:58:43.285 --> 00:58:45.537
Then help us. Fight with us.

445
00:58:45.621 --> 00:58:48.373
Fight with you?
What, join the team? Be an X-Man?

446
00:58:48.457 --> 00:58:51.209
Who the hell do you think you are?
You're a mutant.

447
00:58:51.293 --> 00:58:54.337
The whole world out there
is full of people
that hate and fear you.

448
00:58:54.421 --> 00:58:58.132
And you're wasting your time
trying to protect 'em?
I got better things to do.

449
00:58:58.217 --> 00:59:02.679
You know, Magneto's right.
There's a war coming.

450
00:59:02.763 --> 00:59:06.975
- You sure you're on the right side?
- At least I've chosen a side.

451
00:59:14.733 --> 00:59:18.361
I'm looking for Dr. Jean Grey.

452
00:59:26.996 --> 00:59:29.414
Senator Kelly.

453
00:59:29.498 --> 00:59:31.874
I'm Professor Charles Xavier.

454
00:59:33.794 --> 00:59:37.922
I was afraid if I went
to a hospital, they would --

455
00:59:38.007 --> 00:59:40.049
Treat you like a mutant?

456
00:59:42.136 --> 00:59:46.055
We're not what you think.
Not all of us.

457
00:59:46.140 --> 00:59:49.976
Tell it to the ones
who did this to me.

458
00:59:54.398 --> 00:59:56.357
Senator ...

459
01:00:01.030 --> 01:00:04.532
I want you to try and relax.

460
01:00:07.494 --> 01:00:09.412
I'm not going to hurt you.

461
01:01:01.674 --> 01:01:04.759
Welcome to the future,

462
01:01:04.843 --> 01:01:06.761
brother.

463
01:01:12.893 --> 01:01:17.021
The machine emits radiation
that triggers mutation
in ordinary human beings.

464
01:01:17.106 --> 01:01:19.190
But the mutation is unnatural.

465
01:01:19.274 --> 01:01:21.901
Kelly's body is rejecting it.
His cells began ...

466
01:01:21.985 --> 01:01:24.320
to break down almost immediately.

467
01:01:24.405 --> 01:01:27.281
- What effect does radiation
  have on mutants?
- There appears to be none.

468
01:01:27.366 --> 01:01:31.202
But I fear it will seriously harm 
any normal person exposed to it.

469
01:01:31.286 --> 01:01:35.164
- So what does Magneto
  want with Rogue?
- I don't know.

470
01:01:37.334 --> 01:01:39.794
Wait a second.

471
01:01:39.878 --> 01:01:42.588
You said this machine
draws its power from Magneto ...

472
01:01:42.715 --> 01:01:45.508
and that it weakened him.
- Yes

473
01:01:46.802 --> 01:01:48.886
In fact, it nearly killed him.

474
01:01:48.971 --> 01:01:51.639
He's gonna transfer
his power to Rogue ...

475
01:01:51.724 --> 01:01:54.934
and use her to power the machine.

476
01:01:57.563 --> 01:01:59.731
Is somebody there?

477
01:02:01.567 --> 01:02:04.569
Yes. I'm here.

478
01:02:06.488 --> 01:02:09.490
Please don't leave me.

479
01:02:10.701 --> 01:02:13.119
Don't want to be alone.

480
01:02:14.747 --> 01:02:16.664
All right.

481
01:02:25.632 --> 01:02:28.718
Do you hate normal people?

482
01:02:30.929 --> 01:02:33.598
Sometimes.

483
01:02:33.682 --> 01:02:35.600
Why?

484
01:02:39.354 --> 01:02:41.314
I suppose ...

485
01:02:42.816 --> 01:02:45.151
I'm afraid of them.

486
01:02:47.070 --> 01:02:49.447
Well,

487
01:02:49.531 --> 01:02:53.409
I think you've got
one less person to --

488
01:02:53.494 --> 01:02:55.411
to be afraid of.

489
01:03:18.519 --> 01:03:21.229
Cyclops, you and Storm ready 
the jet. I'm gonna find Rogue.

490
01:03:21.355 --> 01:03:24.440
Jean, get Logan a uniform.
Whoa, wait a minute.

491
01:03:24.566 --> 01:03:27.527
- He's not coming with us, is he?
- Yes

492
01:03:27.611 --> 01:03:30.321
I'm sorry, Professor, but he'll 
endanger the mission. And if-

493
01:03:30.405 --> 01:03:33.533
Hey, I wasn't the one who gave the 
train station a new sunroof, pal.

494
01:03:33.659 --> 01:03:35.952
No, you were the one who stabbed 
Rogue through the chest. Scott --

495
01:03:36.036 --> 01:03:39.413
Hey, why don't you take your 
little mission and stick it up your --

496
01:03:39.498 --> 01:03:41.749
Senator Kelly is dead.

497
01:03:43.627 --> 01:03:45.628
I'm going to find her.

498
01:03:47.297 --> 01:03:49.590
Settle this.

499
01:04:27.296 --> 01:04:29.255
I'm sorry.

500
01:04:52.905 --> 01:04:56.657
You can still hear me, can't you?

501
01:05:04.249 --> 01:05:09.545
You've taught me everything in my 
life that was ever worth knowing.

502
01:05:09.630 --> 01:05:12.965
And if anything happens,

503
01:05:13.050 --> 01:05:16.302
well, I'll take care of them.

504
01:05:29.775 --> 01:05:31.692
Jean?

505
01:05:35.072 --> 01:05:37.490
Jean!

506
01:05:37.574 --> 01:05:39.867
No!

507
01:05:52.714 --> 01:05:54.632
Jean?

508
01:05:54.716 --> 01:05:56.634
Jean.

509
01:05:56.718 --> 01:05:59.053
Answer me. Please.

510
01:06:00.305 --> 01:06:02.264
I know where Magneto's going.

511
01:07:22.095 --> 01:07:24.305
Magnificent, isn't she?

512
01:07:25.557 --> 01:07:30.227
- I've seen it.
- I first saw her in 1949.

513
01:07:30.312 --> 01:07:33.814
America was gonna be
the land of tolerance,

514
01:07:33.899 --> 01:07:35.816
of peace.

515
01:07:40.280 --> 01:07:42.448
Are you going to kill me?

516
01:07:47.788 --> 01:07:50.581
- Yes.
- Why?

517
01:07:50.665 --> 01:07:54.960
Because there is no land of 
tolerance. There is no peace.

518
01:07:55.045 --> 01:07:57.797
Not here or anywhere else.

519
01:07:57.881 --> 01:08:01.717
Women and children,
whole families destroyed ...

520
01:08:01.802 --> 01:08:04.595
simply because they were born 
different from those in power.

521
01:08:04.679 --> 01:08:09.517
Well, after tonight, the world's 
powerful will be just like us.

522
01:08:09.601 --> 01:08:12.645
They will return home
as brothers.

523
01:08:12.729 --> 01:08:15.189
As mutants.

524
01:08:15.273 --> 01:08:17.775
Our cause will be theirs.

525
01:08:17.859 --> 01:08:22.029
Your sacrifice
will mean our survival.

526
01:08:25.742 --> 01:08:29.120
I'll understand if that
comes as small consolation.

527
01:08:32.624 --> 01:08:34.834
Put her in the machine.

528
01:08:36.086 --> 01:08:38.045
I'll raise it.

529
01:08:39.881 --> 01:08:42.883
Magneto is here. Liberty Island.

530
01:08:42.968 --> 01:08:46.345
Now, presumably, his objective
is to mutate the world leaders
at the U.N. Summit ...

531
01:08:46.429 --> 01:08:48.472
on Ellis Island.

532
01:08:48.557 --> 01:08:50.724
He doesn't know his machine kills.

533
01:08:50.809 --> 01:08:54.395
And judging from what the Professor saw, 
if Magneto gave Rogue enough power --

534
01:08:54.479 --> 01:08:58.691
He could wipe out
everyone in New York City.

535
01:08:58.775 --> 01:09:01.944
We can insert here at the 
George Washington Bridge,

536
01:09:02.028 --> 01:09:04.363
come around the bank
just off of Manhattan.

537
01:09:04.447 --> 01:09:07.992
We land on the far side
of Liberty Island here.

538
01:09:08.076 --> 01:09:10.035
What about harbor patrol?
Radar?

539
01:09:10.120 --> 01:09:14.039
If they have anything that can pick 
up our jet, they deserve to catch us.

540
01:09:28.513 --> 01:09:31.515
You actually go outside
in these things?

541
01:09:31.600 --> 01:09:33.976
Well, what would you prefer,
yellow spandex?

542
01:09:40.275 --> 01:09:43.277
Whoa!

543
01:10:24.986 --> 01:10:27.988
Okay, there's the bridge.
I'm taking her down.

544
01:10:34.412 --> 01:10:36.997
Storm, some cover, please.

545
01:10:55.600 --> 01:10:59.270
Toad, Mystique, stay sharp.
We're not alone.

546
01:10:59.354 --> 01:11:01.272
And you stay here.

547
01:11:01.356 --> 01:11:05.109
Once I give my power to the girl,
I'll be temporarily weakened.

548
01:11:05.193 --> 01:11:07.194
You'll be my only defense.

549
01:11:14.786 --> 01:11:16.704
Sounds like a storm's coming.

550
01:11:31.094 --> 01:11:34.596
- Sorry.
- You call that a landing?

551
01:11:46.359 --> 01:11:48.277
The torch.

552
01:11:56.328 --> 01:11:58.579
... within a mile of the proceedings.

553
01:11:58.663 --> 01:12:01.415
The first dignitaries started 
to arrive about an hour ago,

554
01:12:01.499 --> 01:12:03.834
greeted with a sort
of garden-party atmosphere,

555
01:12:03.918 --> 01:12:05.794
which was designed
to entertain them,

556
01:12:05.920 --> 01:12:08.922
as the others
traversed the rigid security.

557
01:12:33.281 --> 01:12:36.992
- There's someone here.
- Where?

558
01:12:37.118 --> 01:12:40.496
I don't know.
Keep your eye open. Logan.

559
01:12:43.583 --> 01:12:46.085
Damn it.

560
01:12:51.966 --> 01:12:54.468
Anything?
I know there's someone here.
I just can't see 'em.

561
01:13:09.025 --> 01:13:10.984
Wait! Wait!

562
01:13:17.450 --> 01:13:19.660
All right, back up. Back up.

563
01:14:34.694 --> 01:14:36.695
Jean!

564
01:14:38.031 --> 01:14:40.115
Oh, God.

565
01:15:40.635 --> 01:15:42.844
Don't move.

566
01:15:58.987 --> 01:16:00.946
Don't you people ever die?

567
01:16:35.356 --> 01:16:38.650
Do you know what happens to a toad
when it's struck by lightning?

568
01:16:45.116 --> 01:16:47.534
Same thing that happens
to everything else.

569
01:17:03.217 --> 01:17:05.135
Logan, is that you?

570
01:17:05.219 --> 01:17:07.179
Shh.

571
01:17:16.981 --> 01:17:20.108
The other one ain't far away.

572
01:17:20.193 --> 01:17:22.694
Come on. We have to regroup.

573
01:17:22.779 --> 01:17:24.738
I know, but there's a problem.

574
01:17:27.325 --> 01:17:30.160
You're not part of the group.

575
01:17:50.807 --> 01:17:52.808
Hey, hey, it's me.

576
01:17:52.892 --> 01:17:56.269
- Prove it.
- You're a dick.

577
01:17:57.480 --> 01:17:59.439
Okay.

578
01:18:01.109 --> 01:18:03.735
Hey.

579
01:18:20.586 --> 01:18:22.879
Everybody get out of here.

580
01:18:23.005 --> 01:18:26.049
What is it?
I can't move.

581
01:18:46.571 --> 01:18:49.239
Ah, my brothers.

582
01:18:49.323 --> 01:18:52.409
Welcome. And, you,

583
01:18:52.493 --> 01:18:55.495
just point those claws of 
yours in a safer direction.

584
01:19:09.594 --> 01:19:11.636
You'd better close your eyes.

585
01:19:14.724 --> 01:19:17.017
- Storm, fry him.
- Oh, yes.

586
01:19:17.101 --> 01:19:21.980
A bolt of lightning into
a huge copper conductor.

587
01:19:22.064 --> 01:19:24.065
I thought you lived at a school.

588
01:19:29.155 --> 01:19:32.699
For those of you who may not be 
familiar with the historical significance --

589
01:19:37.955 --> 01:19:40.665
Mystique?

590
01:19:40.792 --> 01:19:42.876
Mystique?
I've seen Senator Kelly.

591
01:19:44.712 --> 01:19:48.423
So the good senator
survived his fall ...

592
01:19:48.508 --> 01:19:50.884
and the swim to shore.

593
01:19:50.968 --> 01:19:53.178
He's become even more powerful 
than I could have imagined.

594
01:19:53.262 --> 01:19:55.972
- He's dead.
- It's true.

595
01:19:56.057 --> 01:20:00.560
I saw him die. Like those 
people down there will die.

596
01:20:00.645 --> 01:20:04.272
Are you sure you saw what you saw?

597
01:20:04.357 --> 01:20:08.693
I would also like to thank the President 
of the United States of America ...

598
01:20:08.778 --> 01:20:11.029
for hosting this event ...

599
01:20:11.113 --> 01:20:14.533
under the lights of
the great city of New York.

600
01:20:21.874 --> 01:20:25.627
Why do none of you understand
what I'm trying to do?

601
01:20:25.711 --> 01:20:31.466
Those people down there,
they control our fate and
the fate of every other mutant.

602
01:20:32.885 --> 01:20:35.136
Well,

603
01:20:35.221 --> 01:20:37.848
soon our fate will be theirs.

604
01:20:37.932 --> 01:20:41.184
Help! Please help me!

605
01:20:41.269 --> 01:20:43.186
You're so full of shit.

606
01:20:43.271 --> 01:20:47.482
If you were really so righteous,
it'd be you in that thing.

607
01:20:49.360 --> 01:20:53.113
Help! Somebody help me!

608
01:21:05.918 --> 01:21:07.836
Please!

609
01:21:07.920 --> 01:21:12.966
Somebody please help me!

610
01:21:16.846 --> 01:21:19.180
Somebody!

611
01:21:19.265 --> 01:21:21.850
Help --

612
01:21:29.317 --> 01:21:32.861
Logan!

613
01:22:29.710 --> 01:22:33.088
- I'm sorry, my dear.
- Don't do this.

614
01:22:45.518 --> 01:22:47.602
This is mine.

615
01:23:50.499 --> 01:23:52.625
You owe me a scream.

616
01:23:55.963 --> 01:23:58.673
Hey, bub. I'm not
finished with you yet.

617
01:24:01.761 --> 01:24:04.345
Jean.

618
01:24:04.472 --> 01:24:06.890
- Scott, when I tell you,
  open your eyes.
- No.

619
01:24:06.974 --> 01:24:09.476
- Trust me.
- You drop something?

620
01:24:14.023 --> 01:24:16.149
Now.

621
01:24:30.164 --> 01:24:32.373
Thanks. Don't mention it.

622
01:24:32.458 --> 01:24:36.461
We gotta get her out of there.
Cyclops, can you hit it?

623
01:24:36.545 --> 01:24:39.714
- The rings are too fast. I'll kill her.
- Just shoot it.

624
01:24:39.799 --> 01:24:42.092
- Storm, can you get me up there?
- I can't control it like that.

625
01:24:42.176 --> 01:24:45.053
- You could fly right over the torch.
- Then let me go.

626
01:24:45.137 --> 01:24:49.516
If I don't make it, then at least 
you can still blast the damn thing.

627
01:24:50.726 --> 01:24:52.977
All right, do it.

628
01:24:53.062 --> 01:24:55.522
Jean, use your power.
Try to steady him.

629
01:24:56.941 --> 01:24:59.192
Hang on to something.

630
01:25:52.955 --> 01:25:55.081
Scott, wait.

631
01:26:25.696 --> 01:26:28.114
I have to. Just wait.

632
01:26:29.950 --> 01:26:32.535
I have a shot.

633
01:26:32.620 --> 01:26:34.495
I'm taking it.

634
01:27:14.453 --> 01:27:16.371
Come on.

635
01:28:47.338 --> 01:28:50.089
Hey, this one's alive.
Let's get him out of here.

636
01:29:16.200 --> 01:29:18.117
Welcome back.

637
01:29:18.202 --> 01:29:21.245
I knew you'd find your way.

638
01:29:21.330 --> 01:29:23.456
I had you to guide me.

639
01:29:25.667 --> 01:29:27.752
How did we do?

640
01:29:55.197 --> 01:29:57.949
Oh! Oh, that tickles.

641
01:29:59.118 --> 01:30:04.372
Hey.

642
01:30:04.498 --> 01:30:07.792
How're you feeling?
Fantastic.

643
01:30:09.837 --> 01:30:12.213
That was a brave thing you did.

644
01:30:13.632 --> 01:30:17.218
Did it work?
Yeah. She's fine.

645
01:30:18.887 --> 01:30:22.056
She took on a few of your more charming
personality traits for a while.

646
01:30:22.182 --> 01:30:25.810
But we lived through it.

647
01:30:29.273 --> 01:30:32.191
I think she's
a little taken with you.

648
01:30:32.276 --> 01:30:36.696
Well, you can tell her my heart 
belongs to someone else.

649
01:30:41.076 --> 01:30:44.912
You know, you and I --
How's the professor?

650
01:30:47.708 --> 01:30:50.710
He's good. Good.

651
01:30:56.884 --> 01:31:01.137
There's an abandoned military compound 
at Alkali Lake in the Canadian Rockies,

652
01:31:01.221 --> 01:31:03.139
close to where we found you.

653
01:31:03.223 --> 01:31:07.602
There's not much left, but you 
might find some answers.

654
01:31:10.105 --> 01:31:13.274
- Thank you.
- Are you going to say 
  good-bye to them?

655
01:31:16.111 --> 01:31:20.198
The Mutant Registration Act
lost its main proponent today ...

656
01:31:20.282 --> 01:31:22.992
with the dramatic reversal
of Senator Robert Kelly,

657
01:31:23.076 --> 01:31:27.538
who until this time had
provided the loudest voice in
the cry for mutant registration.

658
01:31:27.623 --> 01:31:29.624
I was wrong
on this particular issue.

659
01:31:29.708 --> 01:31:33.002
And I hope in time I may be forgiven.
Thank you.

660
01:31:33.128 --> 01:31:37.757
- The Mutant Registration Act
  continues to draw support ...
- Mystique.

661
01:31:40.093 --> 01:31:43.387
Son of a bitch.

662
01:31:43.472 --> 01:31:47.099
From many "Parents Rights" groups
who feel threatened ...

663
01:31:47.309 --> 01:31:49.227
by unidentified mutants
in their school systems.

664
01:31:49.311 --> 01:31:51.938
In a related story,

665
01:31:52.022 --> 01:31:56.442
the body of Senator Kelly's long-time 
aide, Henry Guyrich, was found today.

666
01:31:56.527 --> 01:32:01.781
Preliminary coroner reports 
seem to indicate that Guyrich 
was mauled by a bear.

667
01:32:01.865 --> 01:32:03.616
Hey.

668
01:32:08.038 --> 01:32:11.499
You running again?
No, not really.

669
01:32:13.168 --> 01:32:16.295
I have some things
to take care of up north.

670
01:32:21.802 --> 01:32:23.970
I kind of like it.

671
01:32:27.140 --> 01:32:30.601
I don't want you to go.

672
01:32:43.115 --> 01:32:45.116
I'll be back for this.

673
01:33:24.197 --> 01:33:26.741
Doesn't it ever wake you
in the middle of the night?

674
01:33:26.825 --> 01:33:29.660
The feeling that someday they 
will pass that foolish la ...

675
01:33:29.745 --> 01:33:34.081
or one just like it
and come for yo ...

676
01:33:34.166 --> 01:33:37.043
and your children?

677
01:33:39.254 --> 01:33:41.547
It does, indeed.

678
01:33:46.845 --> 01:33:49.847
What do you do when
you wake up to that?

679
01:33:49.931 --> 01:33:53.100
I feel a great swell of pity
for the poor soul ...

680
01:33:53.185 --> 01:33:56.854
who comes to that school
looking for trouble.

681
01:34:04.905 --> 01:34:07.531
Why do you come here, Charles?

682
01:34:07.616 --> 01:34:10.618
Why do you ask questions to which 
you already know the answers?

683
01:34:10.702 --> 01:34:13.120
Oh, yes.

684
01:34:13.205 --> 01:34:15.581
Your continuing search for hope.

685
01:34:26.635 --> 01:34:30.930
You know this plastic prison 
of theirs won't hold me forever.

686
01:34:31.014 --> 01:34:35.559
The war is still coming, Charles, 
and I intend to fight it ...

687
01:34:35.644 --> 01:34:37.603
by any means necessary.

688
01:34:39.439 --> 01:34:42.942
And I will always be there,
